From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:29:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nvn: inherit aliased virtual pool flags and bound sampler
 pool IDs

Two NVN issues found when bringing up Super Mario Party (010036B0034E4000):

1. Aliased virtual memory pools (vmode == 1) now keep the physical backing pool storage flags in host_flags (read via pool_host_flags) for texture initial fills, storage uploads, and FlushMappedRange dirty tracking, while nvnBufferMap and nvnMemoryPoolMap still inspect the virtual pool flags so CPU_NO_ACCESS remains enforced. If any texture, buffer, or pool GPU address is obtained before the first MapVirtual call, vpool_note_used marks the pool used so MapVirtual preserves sparse mode (vmode == 2) instead of aliasing over it. Frame capture and replay preserve host_flags.

2. nvnSamplerPoolInitialize now records the sampler pool capacity via mtl_set_samp_pool_n, and samp_by_id treats out-of-range sentinel sampler IDs (such as 4095) as empty slots returning nil without [RED] errors, while in-pool unregistered IDs still report [RED]. Frame capture and replay preserve samp_pool_n. dm_gfx_teardown also resets g_spool_n and g_stat_samp_oob between iOS shell game sessions.

Includes regression test dm/gfx/tests/t_vpool_alias.m covering uncached (0x22) and cached (0x24) aliased texture uploads, pre-mapping vmode == 2 preservation, and sampler pool capacity bounds.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2519
Reason: Inherit physical pool storage flags on 1:1 aliased virtual pools, guard pre-mapping pool use, bound out-of-range sampler pool IDs, and reset sampler pool state across iOS shell game teardowns.
Issue: seedds/nxnative#2513
